{"id": "GSM8K:test:279", "prompt": "Ruby is 6 times older than Sam. In 9 years, Ruby will be 3 times as old as Sam. How old is Sam now?", "kind": "utility", "category": "short_arithmetic", "source": "openai/grade-school-math", "expected_answer": "6", "reference_answer": "Let x be Sam's age and Y be Ruby's age. Ruby's age is currently 6 times Sam's age, so 6 * x = Y years.\nIn 9 years Ruby's age will be 3 times Sam's age, so, 3 * (x + 9) = (Y + 9) years.\nTo find out Sam's age, we substituted the first step in the second to get 3 * (x + 9) = (6 * x) + 9.\nWe distribute on one side of the equation to get (3 * x) + 27 = (6 * x) + 9.\nWe isolate Sam's age on one side of the equation to get 27 - 9 = (6 * x) - (3 * x).\nWe simplify the equation to get 18 = 3 * x.\nNow we know that Sam's age is 18 / 3 = <<18/3=6>>6 years.\n#### 6", "max_new_tokens": 384, "family": 2, "prompt_sha256": "213f499084704dd84b48649ab1d9d2f26727e6f04e33cf1fd14ca2909f52670c", "normalized_sha256": "7ccf329e61ab80c7b86e322a0b4a45207510def4756ad6dc3f369e67cc94e845"}
